# `cp .env.example .env` (gitignored): the local Worker runs on it unedited.
# apps/web's `dev` loads it, a shell variable beating its line, and the Worker
# binds only the names apps/web/cloudflare.config.ts declares. Never create
# apps/web/.dev.vars: the dev server reads it alone and ignores this file.
# Production's secrets are set with `cf workers secrets update`, and its D1's
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_DATABASE_ID and CLOUDFLARE_D1_TOKEN (D1:Edit),
# which @repo/db's push:remote reads, live in .env.production.local.

# Better Auth's signing key: any 32 or more characters locally.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=local-only-better-auth-secret-0000000000

# The scripted Messages API `pnpm dev:web` serves (tools/messages-fake): no key,
# no model. Unset it and set the two below for a real agent, through a gateway
# in your own Cloudflare account that holds your own Anthropic key, never a
# target's, with a spend limit split by the `account` metadata key, the agent's
# one dollar cap (packages/service/README.md § The built-in agent).
ANTHROPIC_FAKE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5177
# AGENT_GATEWAY_URL=https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/<your-account-id>/<your-gateway>/anthropic
# AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Only while a script signs up several users: auth allows 10 requests/60s per IP.
# RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=true

# The connector through a public tunnel, which must pass on X-Forwarded-Proto.
# SITE_ORIGIN=https://<your-tunnel-host>
# __VITE_ADDITIONAL_SERVER_ALLOWED_HOSTS=<your-tunnel-host>
